# Markdown and logs

## Hard rule — every `.md` file

Every markdown file has **both** `## [EN]` and `## [TUR]`.
Keep concept **headings in English**. Explanations follow the section language.

## Where things go

- `days/00.md`, `days/01.md`, … — what we did **that day** and why (both languages).
- `notes/` — concepts, glossary, recall, dated day-close notes.
- Notes names: `00-concept-map.md` style **or** `2026-08-21.md` for a day’s close.
- `experiments/<lab>/` — runnable mini labs + lab README (also EN/TUR).
- Do **not** put Day N work into an older `days/M.md`.

## Current day files (as of 21 Aug 2026)

- `days/00.md` — 19 Aug foundations
- `days/01.md` — 20 Aug neuron, token, attention, transformer, next-token
- `days/02.md` — 21 Aug math map
- Latest close: `notes/2026-08-21.md`

## Style

No Wikipedia. Short cards: definition, why, example, related.
Math this week is **bird’s-eye**: place terms in the system, do not derive everything.
